  "description": "PEMXEN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H96 Ge12 Ho8 N4 O64,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho1B (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2B (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3B (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho4B (Ho) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.716-3.755 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 108.48-110.20°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ho8(phen)2Ge12(μ3-O)24(CH2CH2COO)12(H2O)16]·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 24 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 16 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
